From 08d7185e49ae1ee5ac8e15108edb7be9453a67f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 08:14:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 081/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: validate the ref list
 modification entries

codec_hevc_update_frame_refs() takes ref_pic_list_modification entries
straight from the RPM and uses them to subscript ref_picset0[] and
ref_picset1[], which are MAX_REF_ACTIVE (16) entry arrays on the kernel
stack:

	if (params->p.modification_flag & 0x1)
		cidx = mod_list[i];
	...
	cidx >= num_neg ? ref_picset1[cidx - num_neg] : ref_picset0[cidx];

The index into modification_list[] is bounded - both num_ref_idx_l*_active
are clamped to MAX_REF_ACTIVE, so it reaches at most 31 of 32 entries - but
the u16 *read out of it* is not bounded at all. H.265 requires
list_entry_l0[]/list_entry_l1[] to index the current reference picture set,
yet a corrupt or hostile stream can carry any value up to 65535, reading a
quarter of a megabyte past a stack array. With VMAP_STACK that lands on the
guard page.

Fall back to the unmodified order when the entry is out of range, which is
what the modification_flag == 0 path already computes, so a bad entry costs
the wrong reference rather than an out-of-bounds read.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index b157c52e654a..56f5c64cdc80 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -388,6 +388,17 @@ static void codec_hevc_update_frame_refs(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 		else
 			cidx = i % total_num;
 
+		/*
+		 * list_entry_l0[] is a bitstream field that the hardware RPM
+		 * hands over unvalidated, and ref_picset0/1 are 16-entry
+		 * arrays on the kernel stack.  H.265 requires the entry to
+		 * index the current reference picture set; a stream that
+		 * says otherwise would read hundreds of kilobytes past them.
+		 * Fall back to the unmodified order rather than trusting it.
+		 */
+		if (cidx >= total_num)
+			cidx = i % total_num;
+
 		frame->ref_poc_list[0][frame->cur_slice_idx][i] =
 			cidx >= num_neg ? ref_picset1[cidx - num_neg] :
 			ref_picset0[cidx];
@@ -405,6 +416,10 @@ static void codec_hevc_update_frame_refs(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 			else
 				cidx = mod_list[i];
 
+			/* see the l0 loop */
+			if (cidx >= total_num)
+				cidx = i % total_num;
+
 			frame->ref_poc_list[1][frame->cur_slice_idx][i] =
 				(cidx >= num_pos) ? ref_picset0[cidx - num_pos]
 				: ref_picset1[cidx];
